In article 4545, 13001_6035@uwovax.uwo.ca says:

>I just got NetHack 2.3 from Grape.  I have noticed a large
>number of things I dislike about it.  One or two may be
>bugs.  Perhaps some of them are just misunderstandings.

>1. NETHACK.EXE is BIG!  V2.2 was about 350K, while this is
>   about 440K, making it unplayable without a HD.  I have
>   a HD, but not all my friends do.


One comment from me: please DO NOT cut down the size just to
make NetHack playable from a floppy-only system.  If someone
does not have a HD, they can just play an older version - or,
at worst, put in some #ifdef FLOPPY statements so that you
can create a (wimpy) smaller version.


One more (final) comment: I had a terrific game going yesterday
(-9 AC, intrinsic fire, cold, poison, teleportation, ..., +5
Excaliber), when I got blasted in the hallway by a bolt of
disintegration from an (orange - or whatever the heck it's called)
dragon.  Needless to say, I died instantly.  What's the deal?  At
least a Medusa gives me one move to try something.  I had no warning
in this case.  Is there anything (ie ring of de-disintegration) that
could've helped?



